################################################################################
  >>> PREFERRED: connect from VSCode / Cursor (Remote-SSH to hpc-build01.scidom.de)  <<<
################################################################################

Since the reverse tunnel is already running, port 8171 on the login node
maps directly to Jupyter on this compute node. In VSCode / Cursor:

  1. Open any .ipynb, click the kernel picker (top-right).
  2. -> Select Another Kernel... -> Existing Jupyter Server...
  3. Paste this URL (note: localhost, NOT the compute node):

       http://localhost:8171/?token=81906a0362235fc0fb90e2915effb970c0b0a3b3dfafac8dec8d0a45cddfffa4

  4. Cursor auto-forwards the port to your laptop. Done -- no manual ssh.

################################################################################
  >>> Alternative: use a browser from your laptop                            <<<
################################################################################

-- Step 1: from your laptop, open an SSH tunnel ------------------------------
   ssh -L 8171:localhost:8171 goncalo.pinto@hpc-build01.scidom.de.scidom.de

-- Step 2: open in your browser ----------------------------------------------
   http://localhost:8171/?token=81906a0362235fc0fb90e2915effb970c0b0a3b3dfafac8dec8d0a45cddfffa4

-- Step 3: when done ---------------------------------------------------------
   scancel 35368607

